cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HRMA in academic or published work, please cite it as below."
title: "HRMA: High-Fidelity Rocket Motor Analysis"
abstract: >-
  HRMA is a preliminary-design and educational tool for hybrid, solid and
  liquid rocket motors. It couples equilibrium thermochemistry (Cantera and
  NASA CEA via RocketCEA) to nozzle, internal-ballistics, heat-transfer,
  structural and trajectory models, and exports the resulting geometry to
  STEP, DXF, STL, engineering drawings and OpenRocket motor files. Predictions
  are scored against a git-tracked database of published static-fire and
  flight data by an automated correlation runner. HRMA is not a
  flight-qualification tool; see docs/VALIDATION_STATUS.md for the verified
  envelope, the uncertainty bands and the known limitations before citing any
  number produced by it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Tezgöçen"
    given-names: "Berke"
    email: "btezgocen97@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/berketez/HRMA"
url: "https://github.com/berketez/HRMA"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - rocket propulsion
  - hybrid rocket motor
  - solid rocket motor
  - liquid rocket engine
  - internal ballistics
  - nozzle design
  - combustion thermochemistry
  - preliminary design
